arguments.content:
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the factory-triple constants are now a third copy of `CliConfig`'s defaults**

`_factoryProviderKind` / `_factoryModelId` / `_factoryBaseUrl` duplicate the values already inlined in `cli_config.dart` (constructor defaults, lines 580–582, and the `fromYaml` fallbacks, lines 655–657). If the shipped factory default ever changes, this guard stops matching the new default triple **silently**: fresh configs persist the new triple, `_customProviderBootDefault` returns null, and every new folder boots the factory slot again — the exact bug this PR fixes, with no test failing, because the tests hard-code the current triple too.

Suggest a single source of truth, e.g. expose the triple once and share it:

```dart
// cli_config.dart
static const factoryProviderKind = 'openai-completions';
static const factoryModelId = 'openai/gpt-4o-mini';
static const factoryBaseUrl = 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1';
```

…then reference those from the constructor, `fromYaml`, and `_customProviderBootDefault`. `bin/fah_runapp.dart` already re-states two of the three at the wizard gate (`saved.providerKind == 'openai-completions' && saved.baseUrl == providerCatalog['openrouter']!.defaultBaseUrl`), so the same drift would desync the wizard condition as well — one shared constant set fixes all four sites.

